id: pm-extension-scalar-validation
title: Validate contributed scalar flag values before extension handler dispatch
description: "A harmless echo fixture declares type bool but --enabled not-a-boolean reaches its handler as a string. Coercion preserves invalid input for later validation, yet current dynamic dispatch validates only allowed/required/disabled option keys. Establish an explicit compatible scalar-validation contract for extension authors."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-14T16:21:40.172Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T16:47:27.101Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Define compatibility for invalid number/boolean tokens and optional no-value presence; Apply shared SDK-owned scalar validation before handler invocation where opted in or required by the supported contract; Preserve canonical switch positional behavior and legacy bool grammar; Independently assert malformed value refusals and valid coercion/default/list cases through public CLI/SDK
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "Extension authors can declare scalar validation that rejects malformed boolean and numeric inputs before dispatch while preserving valid aliases, defaults, optional presence and list ordering across public SDK and CLI."
